#!/bin/sh

myip=$(hostname -I | awk '{print$1}')
cat <<EOF
********************************************************************************

Welcome to DigitalOcean's One-Click BTCPay Server Droplet.
To keep this Droplet secure, the UFW firewall is enabled.
All ports are BLOCKED except 22 (SSH), 80 (HTTP), and 443 (HTTPS).

BEFORE YOU CONTINUE:
BTCPay Server requires a domain name pointed at this Droplet's IP
address ($myip) before it can start. This is required for HTTPS.

  1. In your domain registrar / DNS provider, add an A record
     pointing your domain (or subdomain) at: $myip
  2. Wait for DNS to propagate (a few minutes, sometimes longer)
  3. Continue below, the setup wizard will ask for your domain

AUTOMATIC SETUP:
 * The domain setup wizard will launch now (first login only)
 * It checks that your domain actually resolves to this Droplet
   before installing anything
 * Once confirmed, it installs BTCPay Server with HTTPS in one step
 * Bitcoin node is pruned by default (~3 months of blocks, ~25GB)
   to keep disk usage reasonable on a standard droplet
 * If your DNS isn't ready yet, you can exit and rerun it later with:
     sudo /root/configure-domain.sh

For help and more information, visit https://docs.btcpayserver.org

********************************************************************************
To delete this message of the day: rm -rf $(readlink -f ${0})
EOF
